Draft patch — PR #104 briefing includeArchived (CONFIRMED, verdicts.md item 9). The archived-projects query in projects_list joined only project_memberships, so a person whose organization membership was disabled kept listing that workspace's archived projects. Adds the enabled organization_memberships join — the missing half of actor_can_access_project's person branch (the predicate itself excludes archived projects, so it cannot be applied verbatim here). Uncompiled in the authoring sandbox; run cargo check + the briefing integration tests before landing.

diff --git a/apps/server/src/mcp/briefing.rs b/apps/server/src/mcp/briefing.rs
index 623fc72..813c153 100644
--- a/apps/server/src/mcp/briefing.rs
+++ b/apps/server/src/mcp/briefing.rs
@@ -371,6 +371,10 @@ pub(super) async fn projects_list(
                     JOIN project_memberships membership
                       ON membership.project_id = project.id AND membership.actor_id = $1
                      AND membership.enabled
+                    JOIN organization_memberships organization_membership
+                      ON organization_membership.organization_id = project.organization_id
+                     AND organization_membership.actor_id = $1
+                     AND organization_membership.enabled
                     WHERE project.archived_at IS NOT NULL
                     LIMIT 200
                     "#,
